WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.069
What to record on every model call.

2
00:00:02.349 --> 00:00:09.112
The test for a field is simple: will you filter, group, or alert on it, or will you need it to reproduce a problem?

3
00:00:09.392 --> 00:00:11.547
For a model call, these pass the test.

4
00:00:11.827 --> 00:00:14.088
Model requested and model returned.

5
00:00:14.368 --> 00:00:17.547
They can differ (aliases, fallbacks, provider routing).

6
00:00:17.827 --> 00:00:21.432
When quality shifts, the first question is whether the model changed.

7
00:00:21.712 --> 00:00:23.013
Prompt name and version.

8
00:00:23.293 --> 00:00:30.440
Your prompts are code; a version string on every call is what lets you say “quality dropped when triage-v4 shipped.

9
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.003
” Without it, a regression is a mystery.

10
00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:41.944
Tokens, split by kind: uncached input, cache reads, cache writes, and output, plus reasoning tokens where the provider reports them.

11
00:00:42.224 --> 00:00:52.187
Claude’s usage object reports input_tokens separately from cache_read_input_tokens and cache_creation_input_tokens, and each kind has its own price.

12
00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:59.165
Latency: total duration, plus time to first token for streamed calls, because that’s what a user feels.

13
00:00:59.445 --> 00:01:03.627
Cost, computed by your code from tokens and a versioned price table.

14
00:01:03.907 --> 00:01:10.179
Providers don’t put a price on each response, and prices change, so the table belongs in version control.

15
00:01:10.459 --> 00:01:17.179
Finish reason ( end_turn, max_tokens, tool_use, refusal on Claude; other providers use other names).

16
00:01:17.459 --> 00:01:22.472
Truncations and refusals are failures that return HTTP 200.

17
00:01:22.752 --> 00:01:30.219
Tool calls: the tool name and outcome on a child span, with arguments only if your privacy rules allow (lesson 8).

18
00:01:30.499 --> 00:01:37.219
Errors: a low-cardinality error type (such as rate_limit_error or a timeout), and Error status on the span.

19
00:01:37.499 --> 00:01:46.395
Context ids: trace id, a pseudonymous user or session id, the feature or route, and the experiment arm if you’re running one.

20
00:01:46.675 --> 00:01:49.619
Notice what’s missing: the prompt and response text.

21
00:01:49.899 --> 00:01:53.205
That’s a deliberate default, and the next section explains it.
